  "as_of": "2023-08-10",
  "sentences": [
   "The bill would revise employment arrangements for parliamentary staff by clarifying employee categories, workplace principles and the responsibilities of parliamentarians, office-holders and the Prime Minister.",
   "Parliamentarians would assess recruits' capability and gain explicit suspension powers, with consultation and notification requirements involving the proposed Parliamentary Workplace Support Service.",
   "Most amendments would begin 28 days after Royal Assent, while provisions involving the workplace support service would depend on its establishing legislation commencing."
  ],
  "changes": [
   "Generally applicable employment terms determinations would have to be publicly available as notifiable instruments.",
   "Certain electorate staff would avoid automatic termination when their employing minister moves to another relevant office.",
   "Redundant provisions for engaging ministerial consultants would be repealed."
  ],
  "affected": "Parliamentarians, office-holders, their electorate and personal staff and the proposed Parliamentary Workplace Support Service are affected.",
